{
  "description": "deixis mandatory Node[T] attachment vectors — exact fresh attachment of ADR 0010 §5: attach(A,p,k,B) is defined exactly when p ∈ D_A and r = p ++ [k] ∉ D_A; there D_C = D_A ∪ {r ++ q | q ∈ D_B} and v_C = v_A ∪ {r ++ q ↦ v_B(q)}. op \"attach\" gives parent path \"parent\", key \"key\" and subtree \"B\"; its result is {\"defined\": …} or {\"undefined\": {}}. op \"attach-seq\" applies \"steps\" in order. op \"attach-then-at\" and \"attach-then-valueAt\" read the attached tree at \"at\". Every case declares its slot. Hand-authored from docs/design/0010-mandatory-node-values.md, docs/TREE.md and docs/PATH.md as merged in 1a9bb6d, and from nothing else. No implementation of the mandatory API existed when these were written. Items X14 and X15; each note names the defect (W) it catches. 17 cases.",
  "profile": "deixis-mnode-attach",
  "cases": [
    {
